<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niels Juel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1629">1629</a>–<a href="/years/1697">1697</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niels Juel was a Danish-Norwegian admiral, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Christiania</a>, who led the navy of Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scanian-war">Scanian War</a> of 1675–1679. He won a series of victories over the Swedish fleet, above all the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-koge-bay">Battle of Køge Bay</a> in 1677, which gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> command of the Baltic. He is among the most celebrated naval commanders in Danish history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niels-juel.jpg" alt="Niels Juel" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Jacob Coning · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Niels_Juel_(Jacob_Coning_painting).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
